    "statement": "A point particle of mass $0.1\\text{ kg}$ is executing SHM of amplitude of $0.1\\text{ m}$. When the particle passes through the mean position, its kinetic energy is $18 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ J}$. The equation of motion of this particle when the initial phase of oscillation is $45^{\\circ}$ can be given by –",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "$y = 0.1 \\cos\\left(6t + \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "$y = 0.1 \\sin\\left(6t + \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "$y = 0.4 \\sin\\left(t + \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "$y = 0.2 \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} + 2t\\right)$"
      }
    ],
    "source_claimed_answer": "B",
